Z||000000||v8vinnie||02-11-2001||06:05 PM||||well i finnally put on a pair of grabrial premium struts on my v8 87gt, and i also noticed they have a thicker shaft,they also are only 29.99 each with alife time garantee. well they are alot stiffer than the gr2 kyb struts and they control the back end much better, i also installed the poly trans mounts and that stoped the banging i hear under full throttle, but you deffinitly feel a little more vibration from the engine and tranny, but she is finaly handiling the way i want her to, i did notice that the right side shaft is lose in the trans and i guess i better replace the bearing and bushing, this could also add to my vibration and of course the worn and old tires which i will be replacing soon, but at least the rear wobbling is gone, oh! i also fliprd the strut upper mounting plate up side down to get a little more shock travel( per west coast fiero recomendation) it works , also my lowering springs dont move around in the struts when i jack the car up, now i have the front stops to modify, ill let you know a better way to do that real soon too, thalk later!||||reg||1
